verses.text:
Next he took some seed from the land itself
and put it in rich earth.
He placed it like a stream-side tree, next to plenty of water.{a}

It is sharpened to kill many.
It is polished until it flashes like lightning.
Should we celebrate? The rod of My son looks down on every tree.{b}

All My work has worn Me out,{f}
yet the thick crust will not come off.
So into the fire it goes, crust and all!

They will push you down into the pit.{b}
Your death will be violent,
out in the middle of the sea.

You will die like those who were never joined to God’s people,{c}
killed by strangers.
I have spoken, says the Lord Yahweh.”

“Mortal one, sing a funeral song for the king of Tyre. Tell him the Lord Yahweh says:
You were the finished work of a master, perfect,{d}
full of wisdom and perfect in beauty.

You were a guardian angel with a special touch from God.{f}
I set you on the holy mountain of God.
You walked among stones that shone like fire.

You lived a clean life
from the day you were made,
until evil showed up in you.

I will leave Pathros a ruin.
I will burn Zoan,{e}
and Thebes{f} will feel My punishment.

My anger will pour down on Pelusium,{g}
the fortress of Egypt,
and I will cut down the crowd of Thebes.

The young men of On{i} and Pi-beseth{j}
will die by the sword,
and the women of those towns{k} will be taken away as captives.
